# Git runs from  Linux (WSL)

## Context and Problem Statement

Does Git run from WSL or Windows?


## Considered Options

Linux (WSL)
Windows
Both

## Decision Outcome

Chosen option: Linux (WSL)

## Consequences

GitHub no longer accepts passwords over HTTPS, so it requires the use of a token (ssh key) or a different sign-in method. By only using Git from WSL, this needs to be properly setup and tested.
Windows should no longer be used for Git, to familiarize more with Linux CLI.